<title>USA: GOLF-LEADING SCORES FROM TEXAS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING SCORES FROM TEXAS.</headline>
<dateline>IRVING, Texas 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scores after the third round of the $1.8 million Byron Nelson Classic golf tournament on Saturday (players U.S. unless noted):</p>
<p>195 Tiger Woods 64 64 67</p>
<p>197 David Berganio 68 63 66, Dan Forsman 67 64 66, Jim Furyk 63 67 67, Lee Rinker 65 63 69, Mike Standly 66 63 68</p>
<p>198 Brad Faxon 67 67 64, Brad Bryant 65 67 66, Kirk Triplett 67 65 66, John Morse 67 64 67, Chris Perry 65 67 66, Paul Stankowski 64 66 68, Phil Blackmar 68 63 67</p>
<p>199 Hal Sutton 68 65 66</p>
<p>200 Neal Lancaster 70 66 64, Rocco Mediate 66 68 66, Eric Johnson 65 69 66, David Edwards 70 67 63, Andrew Magee 66 65 69, Tom Watson 65 66 69</p>
<p>Add regional scores:</p>
<p>201 Nick Price (Zimbabwe) 69 65 67, Craig Parry (Australia) 66 66 69</p>
<p>202 David Frost (South Africa) 68 68 66</p>
<p>203 Nick Faldo (Britain) 66 68 69</p>
<p>205 Hideki Kase (Japan) 68 70 67</p>
